  <section class="sp-prose sp-sources" id="sources">
    <div class="sp-eyebrow">Sources</div>
    <h2>Where the numbers come from</h2>
    <p>Every bitcoin figure is computed in your browser from the site&rsquo;s shared price series and the Power Law model: trend 1.6&times;10<sup>&minus;17</sup> &middot; days<sup>5.77</sup> since genesis, floor 0.42&times;, upper band 3&times;. Prices are ~12-day closes, measured on 2011 onward as on <a href="/the-bitcoin-floor">The Bitcoin Floor</a>. The live price, when it loads, moves only the readout at the top of the first tab.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Cycle indicators in 2025, including Pi Cycle and the seven of eleven classic top indicators that missed: Galaxy Research, bitcoin cycle report, June 2026.</li>
      <li>The power law&rsquo;s critics and its forecasting record: Baquero &amp; Menezes, &ldquo;Bitcoin&rsquo;s Power Law: Weak Structure, Strong Forecasts,&rdquo; arXiv 2605.21316.</li>
      <li>The doomsday curve: von Foerster, Mora &amp; Amiot, &ldquo;Doomsday: Friday, 13 November, A.D. 2026,&rdquo; <em>Science</em>, 1960.</li>
      <li>Tulip mania: Anne Goldgar, <em>Tulipmania: Money, Honor, and Knowledge in the Dutch Golden Age</em>, 2007.</li>
      <li>Weimar share prices: Costantino Bresciani-Turroni, <em>The Economics of Inflation</em>, 1937.</li>
      <li>Peak-buyer recovery: FRED series NASDAQCOM, NIKKEI225 and CPIAUCSL (Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis); gold from World Bank Commodity Markets (Pink Sheet) monthly averages, via datahub.io/core/gold-prices. Computed 2026-10-04.</li>
      <li>Trend refits in real dollars and gold: the same FRED CPI and World Bank gold series, matched to the site&rsquo;s price samples. Computed 2026-10-04.</li>
    </ul>
